WEBVTT

00:01:32.980 --> 00:01:34.140
Bisco!

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.490
Bisco!

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:47.620
Bisco!

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:57.010
<b>Bow and Arrow Duo</b>

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:57.010
<b>Bow and Arrow Duo</b>

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:19.610
Bisco?

00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:22.010
Yeah.

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:26.580
I heard you. From the 
precipice of the next world.

00:02:31.830 --> 00:02:33.170
You called for me, right?

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:41.680
You're hot! Dummy!

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:43.990
Hot? Me?

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:48.810
Bisco, your body...

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:52.260
What is this?

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:54.240
Bisco!

00:02:58.290 --> 00:02:59.470
Bisco!

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:11.750
Is that... Akaboshi?

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.010
The Rust Eater!

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:18.000
And it's in its complete form!

00:03:18.380 --> 00:03:20.650
How can this be happening?

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:23.960
He's come back...

00:03:24.510 --> 00:03:26.330
as a god!

00:03:43.540 --> 00:03:44.850
Incredible.

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:48.040
What's going on with me?

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:51.250
No matter what arrow I shoot,
 the Rust Eater grows.

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:56.030
This power is welling up inside me 
and won't stop. It's like I'm on fire.

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:59.570
The things coming off you are spores.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:02.970
Which means, right now, you're practically...

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:17.930
Akaboshi...

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:21.790
That bastard's still breathing, huh?

00:04:21.790 --> 00:04:23.020
Wait, Bisco!

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:26.540
I'm coming, too.

00:04:30.490 --> 00:04:32.400
Of course you are, idiot.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.740
Use that, Bisco!

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:44.040
Here we go, Milo!

00:04:44.230 --> 00:04:44.970
Yeah!

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:53.950
Bisco, right now, your blood is 
probably half-human, half-Rust Eater.

00:04:54.280 --> 00:04:57.050
What? You calling me a monster?

00:04:57.230 --> 00:04:59.820
It's because you got drenched 
in the pipe snake's poison.

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:03.700
The Rust Eater spores got into your body 
and mixed with your Mushroom Keeper blood.

00:05:05.290 --> 00:05:08.180
I'm not gonna get it if you 
tell me all this right now.

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:10.590
Defeating that big lug comes first.

00:05:11.350 --> 00:05:15.450
You aren't worried about 
what's going on with your body?

00:05:16.520 --> 00:05:19.330
You understand what's happening to me.

00:05:20.050 --> 00:05:21.070
That's good enough.

00:05:22.860 --> 00:05:25.080
All right, Bisco.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:28.800
Good. This is close enough, Actagawa.

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:34.260
Bisco, wait!

00:05:38.570 --> 00:05:41.610
That thing's bulging like crazy.

00:05:41.610 --> 00:05:43.610
Akaboshi!

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.640
Wait, wait, wait! Don't shoot!

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:47.770
Tirol?

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:51.440
To put it bluntly, that's a sign 
it's about to self-destruct!

00:05:51.440 --> 00:05:56.480
If you shoot it and set it off, you'll end up
 blasting a crater like the one in Tokyo!

00:05:57.020 --> 00:05:58.420
What?

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:02.400
And at this distance, 
Imihama would be wiped out, too.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:06.180
I get that part, but what am 
I supposed to do if I can't shoot it?

00:06:08.040 --> 00:06:11.510
Oh, no! It's about to spew corrosion again!

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:21.770
You did it! Your power is incredible, Bisco!

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:23.740
I can't control it.

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:27.590
Even when I only use a little, 
it blooms like crazy.

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:33.200
Just how much Rust can this thing spew?

00:06:33.960 --> 00:06:37.260
Damn it. We're getting nowhere like this.

00:06:37.260 --> 00:06:40.280
Tirol! Is there any way to stop it?

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:45.550
Hold on! Hold on! Hold on, dummy!
I'm doing my best here, too!

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:50.550
Tracing back from the heart... uh...

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:53.060
If the blood vessels are connected like this,

00:06:53.420 --> 00:06:55.720
then where are its commands coming from?

00:06:56.490 --> 00:07:00.760
It doesn't have an independent AI,
 so how is it self-destructing?

00:07:04.350 --> 00:07:05.640
I got it!

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:08.430
The detonation trigger is the pilot's brain!

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:13.590
That exoskeleton is designed to 
protect the connection to its operator.

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:16.820
If you shoot it through the 
head and kill just the pilot,

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:18.710
Tetsujin won't be able to self-destruct.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.260
Pilot?

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:22.900
Kurokawa...

00:07:23.890 --> 00:07:27.220
Okay! So I just need to 
shoot it through the head?

00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:32.680
Bisco, don't. We don't know where 
Kurokawa is inside that huge head.

00:07:33.190 --> 00:07:38.350
If you miss with arrows that powerful,
 this whole area will go boom!

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:40.850
It's gonna blow up if we just wait around, too.

00:07:41.150 --> 00:07:44.540
Haven't you ever heard the saying, 
"Regret action, not inaction"?

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:49.320
We just need to split that iron mask, right?

00:07:50.050 --> 00:07:52.240
Pawoo, you can't!

00:07:52.540 --> 00:07:55.600
Don't be crazy! 
That's practically a suicide run!

00:07:55.600 --> 00:07:57.490
Actagawa and I will go!

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:01.010
No. A crab can't control its strength.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:06.950
My pole technique has always 
utilized the art of mercy.

00:08:06.950 --> 00:08:11.050
I know how to split armor alone 
without causing shock waves.

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:15.700
Almost as if it were meant 
for this very moment.

00:08:16.330 --> 00:08:18.210
Art of mercy?

00:08:18.570 --> 00:08:21.760
How can you call it that after 
clobbering me like you did?

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:25.200
Milo, your sister seems to 
have no issue with lying.

00:08:25.990 --> 00:08:31.180
That's an awfully rude thing to say when 
I'm heading off to my death, isn't it?

00:08:33.990 --> 00:08:36.670
I'm not a woman of many desires,

00:08:36.670 --> 00:08:40.540
but it's no fun going off to die 
without even a word of thanks.

00:08:41.790 --> 00:08:44.530
What, now? Where's this coming from?

00:08:47.740 --> 00:08:51.570
If you make it back alive, 
I'll give you anything you want.

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:56.110
So don't make that face. You're the
 glorious captain of Imihama Watch!

00:08:57.280 --> 00:08:58.550
Hmm?

00:08:58.850 --> 00:09:01.440
Anything I want?

00:09:14.990 --> 00:09:18.100
That's an advance on taking 
you as my reward, Akaboshi.

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:24.710
She'll definitely make a great wife. 
She's very passionate and well-mannered.

00:09:24.710 --> 00:09:26.150
She's a brute!

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:29.360
Well, you both are, so you're
 perfect for each other.

00:09:29.750 --> 00:09:31.370
Oh, shut up.

00:09:36.330 --> 00:09:39.150
W-Well, I've done everything I can.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:40.670
I'm outta here.

00:09:41.000 --> 00:09:42.140
Thanks, Tirol.

00:09:42.640 --> 00:09:45.690
For risking your life for us.

00:09:45.690 --> 00:09:49.580
I-I'm just repaying you for 
the two times you saved me.

00:09:49.580 --> 00:09:51.690
B-Besides...

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:58.440
If a f-friend... is in trouble, 
you help them, right?

00:10:01.260 --> 00:10:02.450
Akaboshi!

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:05.450
If you die, don't come back as a ghost!

00:10:10.020 --> 00:10:12.590
Jabi-dono, could you launch me?

00:10:19.910 --> 00:10:24.340
Bisco! You and I have 
come a long way, ain't we?!

00:10:24.340 --> 00:10:26.640
Don't let your guard down now, old man!

00:10:26.640 --> 00:10:28.850
If you croak on me in the final hour,

00:10:29.200 --> 00:10:32.260
I'll follow you down to Hell and punch you!

00:10:32.260 --> 00:10:36.090
I've had my fill of jokes
 about the afterlife.

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:39.860
We're finally here, so let's win 
and bring the curtain down!

00:10:40.130 --> 00:10:41.590
Here we go, young lady!

00:10:41.590 --> 00:10:43.360
Want me to say any prayers?

00:10:43.550 --> 00:10:46.900
I'm good. I just helped myself 
to the tongue of a living god.

00:10:49.470 --> 00:10:51.250
What an impressive woman!

00:10:51.710 --> 00:10:53.920
Now go, Actagawa!

00:10:56.900 --> 00:10:59.250
<i>My pole...</i>

00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:03.010
<i>My life... was meant for this!</i>

00:11:12.100 --> 00:11:13.260
Pawoo!

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:31.600
Damn. She actually did it.

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:34.710
Bisco, look!

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:39.240
Kurokawa!

00:11:39.950 --> 00:11:44.660
Akaboshi...

00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:52.230
Hey, Madam, what's going on?

00:11:52.600 --> 00:11:54.200
Shut up and watch!

00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:59.260
Akaboshi...

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:16.750
Phew...

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:19.270
You've gotten a little better, haven't you?

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:23.130
You should praise me like that more often.

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:33.520
Y-You and I a-are the same.

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:41.860
E-Even if you are s-strong and r-righteous,

00:12:43.010 --> 00:12:48.410
I won't just roll over and die, either.

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:53.840
I-I'm... I'm just like you in that!

00:12:56.090 --> 00:12:59.420
Now, disappear!

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:13.110
Go! Bisco!

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:25.430
There are just two rules for using a bow.

00:13:26.060 --> 00:13:27.140
Rule one...

00:13:27.980 --> 00:13:29.650
Keep your eye on the target.

00:13:30.850 --> 00:13:32.100
And the second?

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:34.550
Believe.

00:13:35.380 --> 00:13:37.940
I'll be your eyes.

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:44.070
So believe in me and draw
 the bowstring back hard.

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:47.710
You'll hit it, Bisco.

00:13:48.880 --> 00:13:49.670
Yeah.

00:14:41.740 --> 00:14:44.480
Did we win?

00:14:46.270 --> 00:14:48.620
Hey... Your face!

00:14:53.360 --> 00:14:56.200
It's thanks to your son.

00:14:59.460 --> 00:15:01.200
Hey! It's Bisco!

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:03.070
It's Bisco!

00:15:03.070 --> 00:15:07.590
That fool made me think he 
was dead twice in one day!

00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:08.870
Hmm?

00:15:09.560 --> 00:15:13.020
Are those two unable to get down?
 We can't just stand around here.

00:15:13.460 --> 00:15:14.980
Wait a moment.

00:15:14.980 --> 00:15:15.910
Huh?

00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:19.330
Please just wait a moment longer.

00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:24.140
If we interrupt them now, my little 
brother will never talk to me again.

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:27.990
Wh-What are you talking about?

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:31.530
I can tell. Since we're siblings.

00:15:33.530 --> 00:15:36.520
I originally intended to save two people...

00:15:37.670 --> 00:15:40.530
And look how crazy it turned out.

00:15:40.530 --> 00:15:47.000
With this much Rust Eater, we can cure 
the Rust in Imihama and all of Japan.

00:15:47.310 --> 00:15:50.270
I was always more of a "big picture" guy.

00:15:50.580 --> 00:15:54.010
You sure it's not just because 
you aren't a "details" guy?

00:15:54.310 --> 00:15:57.500
I'm detail-oriented, too.

00:15:57.790 --> 00:16:02.830
You're like those "easy-to-open" 
packets that still refuse to open.

00:16:04.400 --> 00:16:10.730
Is that any way to talk about the 
man who just saved Japan, huh?

00:16:12.050 --> 00:16:13.270
Bisco.

00:16:17.140 --> 00:16:18.730
H-Hey...

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:23.930
I can really hear your heartbeat.

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:29.910
We promised, didn't we?
 That we'd be together when we died.

00:16:30.850 --> 00:16:32.250
Don't...

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:37.640
Don't leave me behind again, Bisco.

